{"seconds": 87.1, "exit": 0, "final": "**Best move: Qg5+**\n\n**Main line:** Qg5+ Kh8 Rxf7 Rxf7 (White wins the f7 pawn)\n\n**Motif:** intermezzo (check wins a tempo)\n\n**Explanation:** Your queen on d5 was hanging to the rook on d6 \u2014 moving it anywhere quiet loses time or material. But Qg5+ is a check, so Black must answer the king safety issue first and can't simply recapture or consolidate. After Kh8/Kh7, the point is that f7 is now undefended, so Rxf7 nets a clean extra pawn. Lesson: when your piece is attacked, first look for a move that both escapes *and* gives check \u2014 forcing moves buy you a free tempo to exploit other weaknesses.\n\n```json\n{\"move\": \"Qg5+\", \"line\": [\"Qg5+\", \"Kh8\", \"Rxf7\", \"Rxf7\"], \"motifs\": [\"intermezzo\", \"hangingPiece\"]}\n```", "tool_calls": [{"tool": "skill", "args": {"skill": "chess-coach"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/3b1p2/pq1r4/1p1Q4/3P3P/1PP2R2/P5P1/2R3K1 w - - 1 29"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-threats", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/3b1p2/pq1r4/1p1Q4/3P3P/1PP2R2/P5P1/2R3K1 w - - 1 29"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-legal_moves", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/3b1p2/pq1r4/1p1Q4/3P3P/1PP2R2/P5P1/2R3K1 w - - 1 29"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/3b1p2/pq1r4/1p1Q4/3P3P/1PP2R2/P5P1/2R3K1 w - - 1 29", "move": "Qxf7+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/3b1Q2/pq1r4/1p6/3P3P/1PP2R2/P5P1/2R3K1 b - - 0 29", "move": "Kh8"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/3b1Q2/pq1r4/1p6/3P3P/1PP2R2/P5P1/2R3K1 b - - 0 29", "move": "Rxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5r1k/3b1Q2/pq1r4/1p6/3P3P/1PP2R2/P5P1/2R3K1 w - - 1 30", "move": "Qxf8+"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "6k1/3b1r2/pq1r4/1p6/3P3P/1PP2R2/P5P1/2R3K1 w - - 0 30", "move": "Rxf7"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-board", "args": {"fen": "6k1/3b1R2/pq1r4/1p6/3P3P/1PP5/P5P1/2R3K1 b - - 0 30"}}, {"tool": "chess-eyes-inspect_move", "args": {"fen": "5rk1/3b1p2